course: dictionary
lesson: 4476
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The context, meaning the words around the word, tells you which meaning the writer wants. The word harpy is a good example: it can name a monster, an insult, or a bird.
explain: In Greek myths, a harpy is a monster with the face and body of a woman and the wings and claws of a bird. In the bird sentence, «The harpy eagle perches on emergent trees», the words eagle, trees and canopy show that harpy means a real bird here.
explain: As an insult, harpy is a rude word for a woman who is thought to be nasty or bossy. It is unkind, so do not use it to hurt anyone. When you read harpy, check the clues: a myth, an eagle, or a person being rude.
fact: Harpy has three meanings: a monster in Greek myths, an insult, and a bird.
fact: The harpy eagle is a huge, powerful eagle of South American rainforests.
fact: The harpy eagle hunts monkeys and sloths in the canopy, the high layer of the rainforest.
fact: «Harpy» as an insult means a woman who is thought to be nasty or bossy, and it is unkind to say it.
fact: Harpy eagles raise only one chick every two or three years, so they recover slowly when they are hunted or their forest is cut.
exercise: «The harpy eagle is one of the most powerful eagles on Earth.» What kind of thing is a harpy here? | A monster from Greek myths | *A bird of prey | A nasty woman | A type of rainforest tree
exercise: In the Greek story, harpies snatch food from people. What is a harpy in a myth? | *A monster with a woman's face and a bird's wings and claws | A huge rainforest tree | A kind old queen | A type of sloth
exercise: Someone calls a bossy girl «a harpy». Why is this unkind? | It means she is a famous eagle | It means she is very tired | It is a compliment about her wings | *It is an insult that calls her nasty
test: «The harpy eagle waits on the tallest tree above the sloths and monkeys.» Which meaning of harpy fits? | An old word for a ship | A woman who is nasty | *A bird | A monster with claws in a myth, the only way to know is to read the rest
test: Where does the harpy eagle live? | Deep underground caves | *South American rainforests | A dry desert | Frozen mountains
exam: Why should you never call a person a harpy? | Because it is the name of a famous ship | *Because it is an unkind insult | Because it is an old word for sloth | Because it means very kind
